From 2ef131b5d1e4cbc0d8b2faeb625a7ef1ca5d6c55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: songliyong <songliyong@huawei.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 15:56:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] US2026033100141 FFIC: Add enhanced crash diagnostics with
 rds_ffic_verbose_crash_diagnostics

Issue:
------
The current implementation of MySQL only prints stack traces during a
process crash; this information is too limited for effective issue localization

Solution:
---------
When rds_ffic_verbose_crash_diagnostics is enabled, handle_fatal_signal()
emits a structured extended crash report covering CPU registers (x86_64
and AArch64) with plain-language hints, stack-top hex dump, instruction
bytes around the faulting PC, FNV-1a crash fingerprint, process memory
stats, loaded executable segments, OS version, and active query context.
All new code is appended to existing files (mysys/stacktrace.cc,
sql/signal_handler.cc); changes to existing code are limited to three
targeted edits in sql/mysqld.cc (SA_SIGINFO registration, global flag,
startup option) and a one-line handler signature change in
sql/signal_handler.cc. All new functions are async-signal-safe.
